<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Emirate of Jabal Shammar</h1><p class="st-meta">1836 CE – 1921 CE · capital Ha'il</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Rashidi emirate of Ha'il, which overthrew the second Saudi state and dominated northern Arabia before losing to Ibn Saud.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1836 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-ibn-rashid">Abdullah ibn Rashid</a> took control of Ha'il, the main town of the Jabal Shammar mountains, with the backing of the Saudi ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faisal-ibn-turki-al-saud">Faisal ibn Turki</a>. His family, leaders of the Shammar tribal confederation, at first ruled as allies of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-nejd">Emirate of Nejd</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Ha'il prospered on the pilgrim route from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> and on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camel</a> and horse trade. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talal-ibn-rashid">Talal ibn Rashid</a> encouraged merchants and building. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-rashid">Muhammad ibn Rashid</a>, emir from 1869 to 1897, intervened in the Saudi civil war, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a> in 1887 and won at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mulayda">Mulayda</a> in 1891, becoming master of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidi-dynasty">Rashidis</a> allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Abd al-Aziz ibn Saud</a> recaptured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a> in 1902 and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-nejd-and-hasa">Emirate of Nejd and Hasa</a> steadily pushed back the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidi-dynasty">Rashidis</a>, killing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-aziz-ibn-mutib-al-rashid">Abd al-Aziz ibn Mutib</a> in 1906. Weakened by assassinations and the Ottoman defeat, Ha'il surrendered to Ibn Saud in 1921 and joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-nejd">Sultanate of Nejd</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/emirate-of-jabal-shammar.jpg" alt="Emirate of Jabal Shammar" width="320" height="221"><figcaption>Image: Guilherme Paula · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Emirate_of_Ha%27il.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1836 CE – 1921 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ha'il</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abdullah ibn Rashid, Muhammad ibn Rashid, Abd al-Aziz ibn Mutib</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a>, <a href="/countries/jordan">Jordan</a>, <a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Emirate of Ha'il, Rashidi Emirate, Jabal Shammar</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1878&amp;focus=emirate-of-jabal-shammar" aria-label="Emirate of Jabal Shammar on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5775 1169 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Emirate of Jabal Shammar lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6095 1425L6241 1527M6095 1425L5709 970M6095 1425L6241 1527"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6241 1527h0M5709 970h0M6241 1527h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6095 1425h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6095 1425h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ha'il. <a href="/atlas?year=1878&amp;focus=emirate-of-jabal-shammar">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

